  "body": "Part of #902. Since #902 the document's unit is the program's unit, and the Heidenhain post refuses an inch document by name (`programUnits = \"mm\"` in `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps`).\n\nThe TNC runs inch (`%NAME G70 *` in DIN/ISO), but the feed unit an inch program and the cycle Q feeds (Q206, Q208, Q253 ...) take was not confirmed from the public manual the post is specced from. A feed off by a factor is no program to post, so it was refused rather than guessed.\n\nDone means: from the published TNC programming manual (behaviour only), the post writes an inch program - `G70` in the first and last blocks, every length / 25.4, every F and Q feed in the unit the manual states, cycle depths/heights in inch - declares `programUnits = \"mm inch\"`, joins `INCH_POSTS` in `crates/app/tests/program_units.rs` with committed inch goldens, and leaves every mm golden byte-identical.\n",
